{"parentUuid":"f88190cc-5dac-439b-8314-30f61c99cf9b","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a434c6a1198c78a5a","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01K1Ahcgkpgtw2BDmdFP6DoU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UnCQg2rWcPuPwPpEnvu2vk","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"column generation 2D facility layout placement Gilmore Gomory pattern"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7261,"cache_read_input_tokens":13121,"output_tokens":196,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7261},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":196,"cache_read_input_tokens":13121,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7261,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7261,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoyR3AN3bgwJEyYgVAVU","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"fdf15b5b-0017-453c-81f4-21f4804f28d4","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:10:16.206Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"f88190cc-5dac-439b-8314-30f61c99cf9b","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"ac68b9dc-9847-4e6f-8ec2-6b4367414408","agentId":"a434c6a1198c78a5a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Kxrnsofm3tdTZxQrruorEG","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"branch and price column generation 2D bin packing strip packing pattern formulation\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"A branch-and-price algorithm for the two-dimensional level strip packing problem | 4OR | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10288-007-0051-7\"},{\"title\":\"A branch-and-price algorithm for the two-dimensional level strip packing problem | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/220340271_A_branch-and-price_algorithm_for_the_two-dimensional_level_strip_packing_problem\"},{\"title\":\"An Evolutionary Algorithm for Column Generation in Integer Programming: An Effective Approach for 2D Bin Packing | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-540-30217-9_65\"},{\"title\":\"A Hybrid Heuristic Based on Column Generation for Two- and Three- Stage Bin Packing Problems | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-319-09129-7_16\"},{\"title\":\"The two-dimensional bin packing problem with variable bin sizes and costs | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/220090491_The_two-dimensional_bin_packing_problem_with_variable_bin_sizes_and_costs\"},{\"title\":\"Exact solution of bin‐packing problems using column generation and branch‐and‐bound | Annals of Operations Research | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1023/A:1018952112615\"},{\"title\":\"A BRANCH-AND-PRICE ALGORITHM FOR BIN PACKING PROBLEM MASOUD ATAEI\",\"url\":\"https://yorkspace.library.yorku.ca/bitstreams/fca85363-6d39-480a-85b2-1830e17d7ee4/download\"},{\"title\":\"Robust Optimization for the Two-Dimensional Strip-Packing Problem with Variable-Sized Bins\",\"url\":\"https://www.mdpi.com/2227-7390/11/23/4781\"},{\"title\":\"[1909.00510] A Geometrical Branch-and-Price (GEOM-BP) Algorithm for Big Bin Packing Problems\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1909.00510\"},{\"title\":\"Models and algorithms for three-stage two-dimensional bin packing - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0377221706003067\"}]\n\nI found comprehensive search results on branch-and-price algorithms with column generation applied to 2D bin packing and strip packing problems. Here's what the literature covers:\n\n## Key Problem Formulations\n\nThe two-dimensional level strip packing problem (2LSPP) consists in packing rectangular items of given size into a strip of given width divided into levels, with the objective to accommodate all items while minimizing the overall height of the strip.\n\n## Methodological Approach\n\nA set covering formulation of the 2LSPP is suitable for a column generation approach, where each column corresponds to a feasible combination of items inserted into the same level, and for exact optimization, a branch-and-price algorithm is used, in which the pricing problem is a penalized knapsack problem.\n\n## Related Formulations\n\nFor the two-dimensional variable sized bin packing problem, an integer-linear formulation is presented, and through Dantzig–Wolfe decomposition, lower bounds of good quality are obtained where the LP-relaxation of the decomposed problem is solved through delayed column generation, with an exact algorithm based on branch-and-price being developed.\n\n## Pattern Generation\n\nColumn generation process can use a hierarchy of methods, including a greedy heuristic, an evolutionary algorithm, and a restricted as well as an unrestricted ILP for the pricing problem.\n\nThe research demonstrates that branch-and-price combined with column generation is a powerful exact methodology for these NP-hard cutting and packing problems, with applications in logistics, glass cutting, and material waste reduction.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"0f85627c-907d-4250-98ef-bcc85787d4e8","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:10:22.451Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f88190cc-5dac-439b-8314-30f61c99cf9b","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"fdf15b5b-0017-453c-81f4-21f4804f28d4","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"ac68b9dc-9847-4e6f-8ec2-6b4367414408","agentId":"a434c6a1198c78a5a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UnCQg2rWcPuPwPpEnvu2vk","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"column generation 2D facility layout placement Gilmore Gomory pattern\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Column Generation MTech Seminar Report by Soumitra Pal Roll No: 05305015\",\"url\":\"https://www.cse.iitb.ac.in/~mitra/mtp/seminar/report/colgen.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Column Generation - an overview | ScienceDirect Topics\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/mathematics/column-generation\"},{\"title\":\"Problems, Models and Algorithms in One- and Two-Dimensional Cutting\",\"url\":\"https://d-nb.info/970782489/34\"},{\"title\":\"A faster variant of the Gilmore and Gomory technique ... - ORBEL\",\"url\":\"https://www.orbel.be/jorbel/index.php/jorbel/article/download/168/124\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction Gilmore and Gomory Model Branch-and-price-and-cut Algorithm\",\"url\":\"https://www.gerad.ca/colloques/ColumnGeneration2008/slides/Carvalho.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Column Generation in Linear Programming and the Cutting Stock Problem | by Bruno Scalia C. F. Leite | TDS Archive | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/data-science/column-generation-in-linear-programming-and-the-cutting-stock-problem-3c697caf4e2b\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) A faster variant of the Gilmore and Gomory technique for cutting stock problems\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/244955595_A_faster_variant_of_the_Gilmore_and_Gomory_technique_for_cutting_stock_problems\"},{\"title\":\"Column generation algorithms - Cornell University Computational Optimization Open Textbook - Optimization Wiki\",\"url\":\"https://optimization.cbe.cornell.edu/index.php?title=Column_generation_algorithms\"},{\"title\":\"Cutting stock problem - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cutting_stock_problem\"},{\"title\":\"Column Generation Model in Capacitated Multi-Periods Cutting Stock Problem with Pattern Set-Up Cost | Science and Technology Indonesia\",\"url\":\"https://sciencetechindonesia.com/index.php/jsti/article/view/266\"}]\n\nI've completed the web search for your query on column generation, 2D facility layout placement, Gilmore Gomory pattern. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Overview of Column Generation and Gilmore-Gomory\n\nIn 1965, Gilmore and Gomory introduced a column generation algorithm for two-dimensional packing problems. The model has a variable for each possible combination of items that fits into a single bin (pattern), and since the resulting Linear Program has a huge exponential number of columns, the Column Generation method starts with a restricted model that only includes a subset of columns and iteratively adds columns that may improve the current solution.\n\n## Application to Cutting Stock Problems\n\nIn 1961 Gilmore and Gomory proposed the delayed column generation technique for the resolution of cutting stock problems, and since then it has been widely used, mainly in one-dimensional cutting problems. The application of this technique to two-dimensional cutting problems has been conditioned by the high computational effort of the auxiliary problems (knapsack problems) resolution.\n\n## 2D Applications and Patterns\n\nTwo-dimensional problems are encountered in furniture, clothing and glass production. The Gilmore-Gomory formulation for 2D-2CP (two-dimensional two-stage constrained cutting) is similar to that for 1D-CSP.\n\nThe search results primarily focus on cutting stock problems rather than facility layout problems specifically. The Gilmore-Gomory approach in 2D contexts has been extensively studied for cutting and packing problems, with column generation being applied through branch-and-price algorithms.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"7510d008-784c-4771-a32e-002dc8c3df67","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:10:23.401Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"fdf15b5b-0017-453c-81f4-21f4804f28d4","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
