{"parentUuid":"43f980a3-23ce-4529-8133-a3e8acfd76d0","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a434c6a1198c78a5a","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01PkPedBrmbUYAE5G4mfzcHJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01M4PKEcproqZA5TnZwPA2rG","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"BaPCod GCG SCIP-Jack branch and price solver framework 2026"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3061,"cache_read_input_tokens":20382,"output_tokens":225,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3061},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":225,"cache_read_input_tokens":20382,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3061,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3061,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoyRts53dqr7BBFBfdcK","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"98731869-60df-40ad-b53a-30d7209b5b93","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:10:29.508Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"1f275925-c741-40a3-af5c-af1d75e722eb","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"ac68b9dc-9847-4e6f-8ec2-6b4367414408","agentId":"a434c6a1198c78a5a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0159Ec3XpvqS5HuW9ULwFKMb","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"stabilized column generation dual oscillation Wentges Du Merle\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Learning to Control Stabilization in Column Generation\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2604.23889\"},{\"title\":\"Detour Dual Optimal Inequalities for Column Generation with\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2108.09233\"},{\"title\":\"In-Out Separation and Column Generation Stabilization by Dual Price Smoothing | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-642-38527-8_31\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Stabilized Column Generation\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/2250769_Stabilized_Column_Generation\"},{\"title\":\"Machine Learning–Supported Prediction of Dual Variables for the Cutting Stock Problem with an Application in Stabilized Column Generation | INFORMS Journal on Computing\",\"url\":\"https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/10.1287/ijoc.2023.1277\"},{\"title\":\"Adaptive Stabilization Based on Machine Learning for Column Generation\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2405.11198v1\"},{\"title\":\"Family Column Generation: A Principled Stabilized Column Generation Approach\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2103.15234\"},{\"title\":\"Stabilized column generation - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0012365X98002131\"},{\"title\":\"Dual Inequalities for Stabilized Column Generation Revisited\",\"url\":\"https://logistik.bwl.uni-mainz.de/files/2018/12/DualInequalities.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Dual-Optimal Inequalities for Stabilized Column Generation | Operations Research\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/abs/10.1287/opre.1060.0278\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about stabilized column generation, dual oscillation, and the work by Wentges and Du Merle:\n\n## Stabilized Column Generation and Dual Oscillation\n\nColumn generation is a widely used decomposition technique for large-scale linear programs, but it often suffers from slow convergence due to poor initial dual estimates and dual oscillations.\n\n## Key Research Contributors\n\nPenalization approaches impose costs for deviations from a reference region using quadratic, linear–quadratic, or piecewise-linear penalties (Du Merle et al., 1999), while smoothing methods (Wentges, 1997; Neame, 1999; Pessoa et al., 2018) post-process the dual values by computing the pricing dual as a convex combination.\n\nDu Merle et al formalized the idea of stabilized column generation in their 1999 paper, which proposed a 3-piecewise linear penalty function to stabilize the column generation.\n\n## Stabilization Approaches\n\nA common framework for smoothing and penalization shows that despite their different mechanisms, both are governed by two design choices: a reference point in the dual space and stabilization parameters that regulate how strongly that reference influences pricing.\n\nAnother widely used approach is to stabilize the dual variables by smoothing, which passes smoothed variables to the pricing problem—a convex combination of the calculated optimum and a stability center (Wentges 1997, Neame 1999, Brunner and Stolletz 2014).\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"60c6cba8-2fbc-40e1-8bdb-b25193ab3853","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:10:35.028Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1f275925-c741-40a3-af5c-af1d75e722eb","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"43f980a3-23ce-4529-8133-a3e8acfd76d0","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"ac68b9dc-9847-4e6f-8ec2-6b4367414408","agentId":"a434c6a1198c78a5a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01REwRKXBxuizRwLD56bG1dw","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"branch and price logic based Benders decomposition hybrid LBBD\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Logic-Based Benders Decomposition for Large-Scale Optimization | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-030-22788-3_1\"},{\"title\":\"Logic-Based Benders Decomposition: Theory and Applications | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-3-031-45039-6\"},{\"title\":\"Stochastic Planning and Scheduling with Logic-Based Benders Decomposition | INFORMS Journal on Computing\",\"url\":\"https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/10.1287/ijoc.2022.1184\"},{\"title\":\"Automatic Logic-Based Benders Decomposition with MiniZinc\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/361528044_Automatic_Logic-Based_Benders_Decomposition_with_MiniZinc\"},{\"title\":\"Combining optimisation and simulation using logic-based Benders decomposition - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S037722172300591X\"},{\"title\":\"Logic-based Benders decomposition for planning and scheduling: a computational analysis | The Knowledge Engineering Review | Cambridge Core\",\"url\":\"https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/knowledge-engineering-review/article/abs/logicbased-benders-decomposition-for-planning-and-scheduling-a-computational-analysis/70EE77BFAE516C56F3363A90A3786D84\"},{\"title\":\"A Logic-Based Benders Approach to Home Healthcare Delivery | Transportation Science\",\"url\":\"https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/10.1287/trsc.2018.0830\"},{\"title\":\"Logic-based Benders Decomposition for Large-scale Optimization J. N. Hooker\",\"url\":\"https://johnhooker.tepper.cmu.edu/LBBDbookChapter.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Logic-Based Benders Decomposition\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/logic-based-benders-decomposition-lbbd-4e47b3ae-690a-44a4-9d80-a191b385b4e6\"},{\"title\":\"Logic-Based Benders Decomposition for Integrated Process Configuration and Production Planning Problems | INFORMS Journal on Computing\",\"url\":\"https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/abs/10.1287/ijoc.2021.1079\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's information about the hybrid approach combining branch and price with logic-based Benders decomposition (LBBD):\n\n## Key Concepts\n\nLogic-based Benders decomposition (LBBD) is a substantial generalization of classical Benders decomposition that allows the subproblem to be any optimization problem rather than specifically a linear or nonlinear programming problem.\n\n## Hybrid Approaches\n\nThe integration of branch and price with LBBD represents an advanced hybrid optimization technique. For routing or vehicle-shift design, master columns are generated via constraint programming or specialized heuristics; LBBD operates in tandem with multiple decomposition layers.\n\n## Branch-and-Check Variant\n\nA key hybrid variant is branch-and-check, which tightly integrates the decomposition with branching. Subproblems are solved within the branch-and-bound of the master; checks and cuts are generated on-the-fly at integer nodes, reducing re-optimization overhead and enabling lazy constraint management.\n\n## Heterogeneous Solver Integration\n\nIn LBBD, the master problem and subproblems can be solved using heterogeneous optimization technologies (e.g., MIP, CP, MILP, specialized algorithmics), with logic-based inference used for generating valid cuts.\n\n## Practical Applications\n\nLogic-based Benders decomposition has improved the state of the art for solving a variety of planning and scheduling problems, in part by combining the complementary strengths of constraint programming and mixed integer programming.\n\nThis hybrid LBBD approach has become particularly valuable for large-scale optimization problems where traditional decomposition methods struggle.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"b73137b2-8339-4e9f-85e3-a599ad3a7b54","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:10:35.584Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"43f980a3-23ce-4529-8133-a3e8acfd76d0","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"98731869-60df-40ad-b53a-30d7209b5b93","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"ac68b9dc-9847-4e6f-8ec2-6b4367414408","agentId":"a434c6a1198c78a5a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01M4PKEcproqZA5TnZwPA2rG","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"BaPCod GCG SCIP-Jack branch and price solver framework 2026\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"The SCIP Optimization Suite 4.0 – Optimization Online\",\"url\":\"https://optimization-online.org/2017/03/5895/\"},{\"title\":\"Solving process of GCG | Download Scientific Diagram\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/figure/Solving-process-of-GCG_fig1_221131622\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Automatic Decomposition and Branch-and-Price—A Status Report\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/268366109_Automatic_Decomposition_and_Branch-and-Price-A_Status_Report\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) BaPCod - a generic branch-and-price code\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/355928331_BaPCod_-_a_generic_branch-and-price_code\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - scipopt/gcg · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/scipopt/gcg\"},{\"title\":\"The SCIP Optimization Suite 8.0 Ksenia Bestuzheva · Mathieu Besan¸con\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2112.08872\"},{\"title\":\"Using SCIP GCG in JuMP - Optimization (Mathematical) - Julia Programming Language\",\"url\":\"https://discourse.julialang.org/t/using-scip-gcg-in-jump/55770\"},{\"title\":\"Implementing the branch-and-cut approach for a general purpose Benders’ decomposition framework - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0377221720307505\"},{\"title\":\"GCG: A Generic Branch-Price-and-Cut Solver - TRISTAN\",\"url\":\"https://tristanconference.org/system/tristan-viii/book_of_abstracts/data/Methodological/TRISTAN8_paper_164.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"2: Solving process of GCG | Download Scientific Diagram\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/figure/Solving-process-of-GCG_fig2_320625000\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about these optimization solvers and frameworks:\n\n## BaPCod\n\nBaPCod is a C++ library implementing a generic branch-cut-and-price solver. BaPCod was developed in Bordeaux University and Bordeaux Research Center of Inria, France. It includes the VRPSolver extension which allows one to model and efficiently solve a large number of vehicle routing and related problems.\n\n## GCG\n\nGCG is currently one of the only available open-source solvers for mixed integer programming (MIP) that applies a comprehensive and expandable Branch-Price-and-Cut framework. GCG extends SCIP to automatically detect problem structure and generically apply decomposition algorithms based on the Dantzig-Wolfe or the Benders' decomposition scheme.\n\n## SCIP-Jack\n\nSCIP-Jack is an extension of the SCIP framework for solving Steiner tree problems. Additional problem classes and major performance improvements are available in SCIP-Jack.\n\n## Connection Between the Tools\n\nThe SCIP Optimization Suite consists of the branch-cut-and-price framework and mixed-integer programming solver SCIP, the linear programming solver SoPlex, the modeling language Zimpl, the parallelization framework UG, and the generic branch-cut-and-price solver GCG. BaPCod, along with other solvers, are still in their infancy with respect to solving general MIPs with block structure.\n\nThe search results do not contain specific information about developments or releases in 2026.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"6a392901-af28-4ad3-8bd3-698a7975ae9b","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:10:36.549Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"98731869-60df-40ad-b53a-30d7209b5b93","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
