{"parentUuid":"8b915506-9fb0-447a-b8cd-a8756799aa43","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a434c6a1198c78a5a","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01JQ4SjCCYB4DUav5bGtyufX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JieH3aD4xpvHA91zrKK5de","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"\"branch and price\" \"facility location\" 2D grid placement LP relaxation tightening"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4237,"cache_read_input_tokens":23443,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4237,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":44,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoySs7Rdgd8Cabx1MG46","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"e64b0f65-4a06-4fd1-80c9-8a68ef4e2c18","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:10:40.942Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"8b915506-9fb0-447a-b8cd-a8756799aa43","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"ac68b9dc-9847-4e6f-8ec2-6b4367414408","agentId":"a434c6a1198c78a5a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01M5yyVZn8cjtZXPniGsGm4t","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"column generation rectangle packing configuration based pricing problem placement\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Scaling Bin Packing: Column Generation in Action | by tejas ghorpade | Suboptimally Speaking | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/suboptimally-speaking/scaling-bin-packing-column-generation-in-action-25f72bd24f12\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - fontanf/columngenerationsolver: A solver based on column generation · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/fontanf/columngenerationsolver\"},{\"title\":\"Integer programming column generation: accelerating branch-and-price using a novel pricing scheme for finding high-quality solutions in set covering, packing, and partitioning problems | Mathematical Programming Computation | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s12532-023-00240-w\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) A column generation-based heuristic for the three-dimensional bin packing problem with rotation\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/314657085_A_column_generation-based_heuristic_for_the_three-dimensional_bin_packing_problem_with_rotation\"},{\"title\":\"Branch-and-Price: Column Generation for Solving Huge Integer Programs | Operations Research\",\"url\":\"https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/10.1287/opre.46.3.316\"},{\"title\":\"The two-dimensional bin packing problem with variable bin sizes and costs - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1572528605000216\"},{\"title\":\"[2202.12466] A Data-Driven Column Generation Algorithm For Bin Packing Problem in Manufacturing Industry\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2202.12466\"},{\"title\":\"Exact algorithms for class-constrained packing problems - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0360835220301893\"},{\"title\":\"Column generation algorithms - Cornell University Computational Optimization Open Textbook - Optimization Wiki\",\"url\":\"https://optimization.cbe.cornell.edu/index.php?title=Column_generation_algorithms\"},{\"title\":\"Optimizing with Column Generation\",\"url\":\"https://optimization-online.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/Book_on_Column_Generation___Part_I.pdf\"}]\n\nI've performed a web search for your query about column generation, rectangle packing, configuration-based pricing, and placement problems. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Column Generation in Packing Problems\n\nColumn generation is used to solve packing problems by generating promising patterns dynamically. The approach uses dual values from the Restricted Master Problem to find new, promising patterns via a pricing problem.\n\n## Pricing Problem in Rectangle Packing\n\nIn geometric packing problems, fast column generation is carried out by applying a heuristic pricing method, in which items with most negative reduced cost are sequentially positioned into bins based on an extreme point concept.\n\n## Configuration-Based Approaches\n\nThe two-dimensional variable sized bin packing problem involves packing rectangular items into rectangular bins with different sizes and costs, with the objective to minimize the overall cost of bins used for packing the rectangles. Dantzig–Wolfe decomposition enables obtaining high-quality lower bounds, with the LP-relaxation solved through delayed column generation and an exact algorithm based on branch-and-price.\n\n## Data-Driven Extensions\n\nAdvanced constraint handling strategies exploit historical packing records with the most negative reduced cost values, since constraints have been implicitly satisfied in these records, thus saving computational load.\n\nThese approaches are fundamental to solving complex packing and placement optimization problems efficiently at scale.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"5a2cbb78-869e-4abd-84ec-51f469b3a1dc","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:10:47.649Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8b915506-9fb0-447a-b8cd-a8756799aa43","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"e64b0f65-4a06-4fd1-80c9-8a68ef4e2c18","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"ac68b9dc-9847-4e6f-8ec2-6b4367414408","agentId":"a434c6a1198c78a5a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JieH3aD4xpvHA91zrKK5de","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"branch and price\" \"facility location\" 2D grid placement LP relaxation tightening\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Facility location problem - Cornell University Computational Optimization Open Textbook - Optimization Wiki\",\"url\":\"https://optimization.cbe.cornell.edu/index.php?title=Facility_location_problem\"},{\"title\":\"A Branch-and-Price Algorithm for Facility Location with ...\",\"url\":\"https://ira.lib.polyu.edu.hk/bitstream/10397/89798/1/Song_Branch-and-price_Algorithm_Facility.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"A Branch-and-Price Algorithm for Facility Location with General Facility Cost Functions | INFORMS Journal on Computing\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1287/ijoc.2019.0921\"},{\"title\":\"A branch-and-price algorithm for the capacitated facility location problem | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/223864238_A_branch-and-price_algorithm_for_the_capacitated_facility_location_problem\"},{\"title\":\"A branch-and-price algorithm for the robust single-source capacitated facility location problem under demand uncertainty - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2192437621000340\"},{\"title\":\"A branch-and-price algorithm for the capacitated facility location problem - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0377221706000828\"},{\"title\":\"Facility location problems — Mathematical Optimization: Solving Problems using Gurobi and Python\",\"url\":\"https://scipbook.readthedocs.io/en/latest/flp.html\"},{\"title\":\"An Exact Column Generation Approach to the Capacitated Facility Location Problem | Springer Nature Link (formerly SpringerLink)\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-642-17020-1_1\"},{\"title\":\"An efficient branch-and-cut approach for large-scale competitive facility location problems with limited choice rule\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2406.05775\"},{\"title\":\"Branch and bound for the fixed-shape unequal area facility layout problem - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0360835225001330\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about branch-and-price algorithms for facility location problems. Here's what the research shows:\n\n## Branch-and-Price for Facility Location\n\nBranch-and-price algorithms for facility location problems utilize column generation and demonstrate more stable performance across various problem sizes compared to branch-and-bound methods.\n\nA branch-and-price algorithm for the capacitated facility location problem is based on a Lagrangean relaxation of the demand constraints and a stabilized column generation method for solving the corresponding master problem to optimality.\n\n## LP Relaxation Tightening\n\nThe search results address the importance of tightening LP relaxations:\n\nThere is a trade-off between shorter times for solving linear optimization relaxations in weaker formulations and longer computational times for branch-and-bound, with stronger formulations being more desirable as the enumeration tree grows very rapidly.\n\nRecent work demonstrates that tight LP relaxations significantly improve algorithm performance, and lifted submodular inequalities can be stronger than classic submodular inequalities, leading to tighter LP relaxations.\n\n## 2D Grid Placement\n\nThe search results mention grid-based approaches: Grid-based network planning strategies using a three-tier (Macro-Meso-Micro) approach have been applied for facility placement, with the macro-level covering entire cities and the meso-level assessing detailed routes.\n\nHowever, the search results don't contain extensive specific information combining all these elements (branch-and-price, 2D grid placement, and LP relaxation tightening methods) in a single integrated framework.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"3b60f4ca-d242-4bc1-86c3-46f11bd88bf2","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:10:47.842Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e64b0f65-4a06-4fd1-80c9-8a68ef4e2c18","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"3b60f4ca-d242-4bc1-86c3-46f11bd88bf2","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a434c6a1198c78a5a","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01A4p2peEBPaGvjGhQtKLMXe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have enough material now. Let me synthesize the research findings.\n\n# Branch-and-Price / Column Generation 调研：用于 2D placement 的可行性\n\n## 1. 经典公式：B&P for 2D bin/strip packing\n\n最经典是 Gilmore-Gomory (1961/1965) 的 set-covering / cutting-stock 公式，每列对应\"一个 pattern\"——即一个可行的物品组合。\n\n- **2D level strip packing (2LSPP)**: 每条 level（水平条带）= 一个 column，pricing 是 penalized knapsack (Lodi/Monaci)\n- **2D variable-sized bin packing**: 每个 bin 配置 = 一个 column，Dantzig-Wolfe 分解后用 delayed column generation\n- **3D bin packing**: pricing 用 extreme-point 启发式 + 序列放置\n\n核心特征：**items 是离散的、可枚举的**，pattern 空间虽然指数级大但每个 pattern 内部几何独立。\n\n## 2. Pattern-based column 形式（关键候选）\n\n最相关的几种 pattern 选择：\n\n- **Line/level pattern**: 每条水平/垂直线上的物品组合（2-stage cutting 标准做法）\n- **Region pattern**: 把 grid 切成可行子矩形，每个子矩形里塞东西\n- **Configuration column**: 每个 column 是\"一个完整的局部布局方案\"（包含 facility + 其周围绑定/路由）\n\n我们的语境最贴近 **configuration column**：每个 column = 一个 facility cluster 的完整放置方案（位置 + 绑定 + 局部路由），master 选哪些 cluster 共存。\n\n## 3. Stabilized CG（Du Merle 1999, Wentges 1997）\n\n朴素 CG 在退化 LP 上会 dual 振荡、tailing-off 严重。三种主流稳定化：\n- **Penalty-based**（Du Merle）：dual 偏离 reference 时加 3-段折线惩罚\n- **Smoothing**（Wentges/Neame）：pricing 用历史 dual 的凸组合\n- **In-out separation / dual price smoothing**（Pessoa 2018）\n\n近年 ML-supported dual prediction（INFORMS JoC 2024）能直接预测稳定 dual 起点。\n\n## 4. B&P + LBBD 混合\n\nLBBD 文献明确支持：master 用 B&P 生成 column，subproblem 用 CP/MIP/专用算法做 feasibility 检验并产生 logic-based cut（Hooker 2019 章节）。**Branch-and-check** 变体把 subproblem 检查嵌入分支树整数节点，避免重复解 master。这正好是我们 binding/routing/flow 链的位置。\n\n## 5. 现代工具\n\n- **GCG** (scipopt/gcg)：开源，自动检测 block structure 应用 Dantzig-Wolfe；目前唯一开源通用 BP&C 框架\n- **BaPCod** (Inria Bordeaux)：C++ 通用框架，含 VRPSolver\n- **SCIP-Jack**：Steiner tree 专用，跟我们无关\n- **columngenerationsolver** (fontanf, GitHub)：轻量级 C++ 模板\n\n**没有原生 Python 接口**：BaPCod / GCG 都是 C++，集成成本高。我们当前 OR-Tools CP-SAT 栈不直接兼容。\n\n## 6. 跟 binding/routing 的对偶关系\n\n- **Benders（我们现在）**：master 决策 → subproblem 给 cut 反馈 → master 收紧。Cut = 行（约束）。\n- **B&P**：master 选列（pattern） → pricing 生成新列 → master 扩展。Column = 列（变量）。\n\n二者**不矛盾，是对偶**。Benders 在\"约束空间\"工作，B&P 在\"变量空间\"工作。可以同一个 master 同时做 B&P（生成新 facility cluster 配置）+ Benders（接受 binding/routing/flow 反馈剪枝）——文献里叫 **branch-price-and-Benders-cut**。\n\n## 7. Master LP 松弛能否被 B&P 收紧？\n\n**理论上能，但前提是 column 的几何意义比 grid-cell 强**。我们 master 现在松弛弱的根因是：facility 占位 + ghost rectangle 用单元格指示变量表达，LP 松弛可以\"分数化占位\"。\n\n如果换成 **configuration column**（每个 column = 一组 facility 的完整紧凑放置 + 内部端口配对），LP 松弛对应\"分数化选 cluster\"——分数解的几何意义更强，松弛更紧。这是 Dantzig-Wolfe 的标准收益。\n\n但代价：pricing problem 本身就是**带几何约束的子问题**——基本等价于\"小规模 placement 子题\"，在 70x70、266 个强制实例下，pricing 自己就可能很难。\n\n## 是否值得 PoC + 具体公式建议\n\n**结论：值得做小规模 PoC，但不替换 Benders，作为补强 master 松弛的并行实验。**\n\n**风险评估**：\n- 高风险：266 个 mandatory + 70x70 + ghost rectangle 几何约束让 pricing 子问题接近原问题，可能没收益\n- 中风险：开源工具栈与 Python/CP-SAT 不亲，集成成本 1-2 周\n- 低风险：跟现有 certified_exact 路径完全隔离，B&P 当 exploratory lane 就行\n\n**具体公式建议（PoC v0）**：\n1. **Column 定义**：每个 column = 一个 \"facility cluster\"（K=2~5 个 facility 的紧凑放置方案 + 内部端口绑定 + 内部路由可行性证明）\n2. **Master**: set-partition over mandatory facility instances + ghost rectangle 几何约束（保留为显式行）\n3. **Pricing**: 小型 CP-SAT 子模型，对每种 cluster 模板枚举 anchor 位置，目标 = -sum(dual_i for facility i in cluster) + cluster_offset_dual\n4. **Stabilization**: Wentges smoothing（实现最简单，0.5 凸组合起步），观察 dual 稳定性后再考虑 Du Merle 3-段惩罚\n5. **不做 branch**：先只做 root-node CG，看 LP 松弛比当前 master LP 紧多少。**只有 LP gap 缩小 ≥30%** 才进入 B&P 阶段\n6. **工具选择**：用 Python + OR-Tools CP-SAT 自己写最朴素 CG loop，不引 GCG/BaPCod；如 PoC 有效再考虑\n\n**Go/No-Go 阈值**（PoC 后 1 周决定）：\n- LP relaxation gap 缩小 ≥30% → 推进 B&P\n- 缩小 10-30% → 只用 root CG 当 bound generator，不做完整 B&P\n- 缩小 <10% → 放弃，pricing 几何耦合太强，B&P 不适合本问题\n\n**与 Phase 3B Lane B（deterministic tuning）的关系**：B&P PoC 应该走 Lane C（exploratory），明确不写 checkpoint、不影响 certified path，符合 AI Safety Contract 类似的隔离原则。\n\nSources:\n- [Branch-and-price for 2D level strip packing (4OR)](https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10288-007-0051-7)\n- [Geometrical Branch-and-Price (GEOM-BP) for big bin packing](https://arxiv.org/abs/1909.00510)\n- [Stabilized Column Generation (Du Merle et al.)](https://www.researchgate.net/publication/2250769_Stabilized_Column_Generation)\n- [Wentges smoothing / In-Out separation](https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-642-38527-8_31)\n- [Logic-Based Benders Decomposition (Hooker, 2019)](https://johnhooker.tepper.cmu.edu/LBBDbookChapter.pdf)\n- [GCG Generic Branch-Price-and-Cut](https://github.com/scipopt/gcg)\n- [BaPCod generic branch-and-price code](https://www.researchgate.net/publication/355928331_BaPCod_-_a_generic_branch-and-price_code)\n- [Branch-and-Price: Column Generation for Huge IPs (Barnhart et al.)](https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/10.1287/opre.46.3.316)\n- [Branch-and-price for capacitated facility location](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0377221706000828)\n- [ML-supported dual prediction for stabilized CG (INFORMS JoC)](https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/10.1287/ijoc.2023.1277)"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2911,"cache_read_input_tokens":27680,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2911,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoyThJMZBMmPpnYeirmx","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"f0c5c9bc-4bcf-405c-be11-2781b58fbd12","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:11:47.579Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
